    "rawText": "Invitation→Journal WritetoSee Putting experience into words is one of the most researched ways to step out. Psychologist James Pennebaker spent decades studying what happens when people write honestly about emotionally significant experiences (life transitions, job changes,andmoreEven15minutes aday,across aboutfourdays,is linked to improvements in well-being and the ability tomove forward. The key wasn't catharsis or venting.It was the act of translating raw experience into language,which creates just enough distance between the thinker and the thought to see things differently. STEPPINGOUT 57",
    "htmlContent": "<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Invitation→Journal</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">WritetoSee</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Putting experience into words is one of the most researched ways to step out.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Psychologist James Pennebaker spent decades studying what happens when</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">people write honestly about emotionally significant experiences (life transitions,</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">job changes,andmoreEven15minutes aday,across aboutfourdays,is linked</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">to improvements in well-being and the ability tomove forward.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">The key wasn't catharsis or venting.It was the act of translating raw experience</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">into language,which creates just enough distance between the thinker and the</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">thought to see things differently.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">STEPPINGOUT 57</p>"
