    "lineCount": 20,
    "rawText": "Bothness is: ·Holding twotruthswithout lettingone erase theother ·Stayingwith thetensionrather thanrushing toresolveit Avisibiltypracticenotasolution Bothness \"Two sides to everything\":bothness doesn't apply to harm Relativism:a fact anda counterclaim don't getequal status Acallforcomprorise:youcanhold both truths and still or dehumanization.We hold safety anddignityfirst isnot: Forced balance:one truthmay mattermore in a context; choose a firm course bothnessjustkeeps the other visible Pocket Practice Welcome In 60 secondsor less Dissent One person can hold two truths at once.So can a conversation,when we keep both alive instead of collapsing to one.Welcoming dissent is how. After sharing an idea or during a discussion: Ask openly:“Who can offer a dissenting perspective？” Thank the first voice that speaks up. ·Avoid:“Who agrees?\" It pulls the room toward consensus before alternatives surface. ·Avoid:“Who disagrees?”It labels the person rather than the idea, which reduces psychological safety and learning. Show Up Step Out WalkYourWhy Move On 68 @2026SUSANDAVID·EMOTIONALAGILITY@·VERSION 2.0",
    "htmlContent": "<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Bothness is: ·Holding twotruthswithout lettingone erase theother ·Stayingwith thetensionrather thanrushing toresolveit Avisibiltypracticenotasolution</p>\n<div class=\"guide-card card-hold\"><div class=\"card-badge\">🛑 HOLD (留白·不劇透)</div><div class=\"card-body\">Bothness &quot;Two sides to everything&quot;:bothness doesn't apply to harm Relativism:a fact anda counterclaim don't getequal status Acallforcomprorise:youcanhold both truths and still or dehumanization.We hold safety anddignityfirst</div></div>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">isnot: Forced balance:one truthmay mattermore in a context; choose a firm course</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">bothnessjustkeeps the other visible</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Pocket Practice</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Welcome In 60 secondsor less</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Dissent One person can hold two truths at once.So can a conversation,when we</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">keep both alive instead of collapsing to one.Welcoming dissent is how.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">After sharing an idea or during a discussion:</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Ask openly:“Who can offer a dissenting perspective？” Thank the</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">first voice that speaks up.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">·Avoid:“Who agrees?&quot; It pulls the room toward consensus before</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">alternatives surface.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">·Avoid:“Who disagrees?”It labels the person rather than the idea,</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">which reduces psychological safety and learning.</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Show Up</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Step Out</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">WalkYourWhy</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">Move On</p>\n<p class=\"guide-paragraph\">68 @2026SUSANDAVID·EMOTIONALAGILITY@·VERSION 2.0</p>"
