    "rawText": "EvidenceBase Why ThisWorks Reflecting on personal values is associated with reduced neural stress responses and sustained self-management under pressure. Dutcher,Eisenberger,Woo,Klein,Harris,Levine&Creswell (2020) —Reflecting on personal values activated reward-related brain regions and reduced activity in threat-related regions duringa stressfultask. ·Schmeichel &Vohs(2009)—Affirming core values restored self- management after sustained effort. Whenwewalkourwhy,whatwevaluebecomes howwe live.Howwe live becomes the cultureswehelpcreate. 93 WALKINGYOURWHY",
