    "rawText": "Evidence Base Why This Works Valuesaligned goalsmallrpeated actionsand intentionallanning are the conditions underwhich lasting change becomes possible. Deci& Ryan (200o)-Goals driven by intrinsic values(growth, connection,contribution) sustainmotivation and well-being over time; goals driven by external pressure deplete energy and increase the likelihoodof giving up. Milyavskaya,Inzlicht,Hope&Koestner(2015)-Goalspursued for want-to reasonsmeet fewer and weaker temptations and are more often attained;theadvantage liesinreduced temptation,notgreatr self-control. Lally,vanJaarsveld,Potts&Wardle(2010)—Habitsformthrough consistent repetition in stable contexts; small actions repeated regularlybecome automatic over time. Gollwitzer (1999) —Forming specific if-then plans(when X happens, I will do Y) significantly increases follow-through by reducing the decision-making required in themoment. Wrzesniewski&Dutton(2001)—Peoplereshape thejob they alreadyhave by adjusting tasks,interactions,and how they see it; this crafting is linked to changed work meaning and identity. See:House of Change adapted from Grant & Greene (2001),Coach Yourself: Make Real Changes in Your Life (Pearson Education). A story can authorus.With Emotional Agility,we authorit. 113 MOVINGON",
